Hungry Bhārgava returns with disciples to hermitage --- Bhārgava sees dust-stained Arajā like eclipsed moonlight --- Bhārgava curses Daṇḍa to death with army in seven nights --- Bhārgava dooms his hundred-yōjana realm to dust rain --- Hermitage folk leave realm and settle beyond borders at his order --- Bhārgava bids Arajā dwell fearless by nearby lake --- Bhārgava departs elsewhere while curse burns realm to ash --- Land becomes Daṇḍakāraṇya housing Janasthāna ascetics --- Agastya ends tale and sends Rāma to evening worship